  "worked_solution": "Recall that the Euclidean distance is defined as\n\n$$\n{d}_{2}(a,b)=‖a-b{‖}_{2}\n$$\n\nwhere for an $N$-dimensional vector $v,$\n\n$$\n‖v{‖}_{2}=\\sqrt{{\\sum }_{i=1}^{N}|{v}_{i}{|}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{d}_{2}(a,b) & =‖a-b{‖}_{2} \\\\  & ={‖[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]‖}_{2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{|2-5{|}^{2}+|6-3{|}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{18} \\\\  & ≈4.243.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
